 FAST ENERGY REGION                                               7434 1451
 Authors: R. Capote, A. Trkov, E. Soukhovitskii                   7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                7434 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               7434 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              7434 1451
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-2.19b35 by                    7434 1451
 M. Herman et al [He01, He02]. This code integrates               7434 1451
 into a single system a number of important modules               7434 1451
 and features:                                                    7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 7434 1451
   coupled-channels (ECIS03 by J. Raynal)                         7434 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    7434 1451
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              7434 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                7434 1451
   TRISTAN by H. Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                      7434 1451
 - Exciton model with angular momentum coupling                   7434 1451
   (code DEGAS by E. Betak and P. Oblozinsky) that                7434 1451
   represents a good approximation to the DSD model               7434 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      7434 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 7434 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                7434 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   7434 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                7434 1451
   discrete transitions                                           7434 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL-2 library [Ri03]              7434 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                7434 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               7434 1451
   and gamma strength functions  based on the RIPL-2              7434 1451
   library [Ri03]                                                 7434 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              7434 1451
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           7434 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    7434 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 7434 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                7434 1451
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      7434 1451
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        7434 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 7434 1451
 current evaluation:                                              7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-2 level                 7434 1451
 file, based on the 1998 version of ENSDF.                        7434 1451
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  7434 1451
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      7434 1451
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            7434 1451
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           7434 1451
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS set to  1.3 (Recommended ~ 1.57434 1451
 Max hole number in PCROSS set to 0.30*sqrt(g*U)                  7434 1451
    being U the CN excitation energy                              7434 1451
 Width fluctuations calculated within HRTW  up to 2.00 MeV        7434 1451
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  1             7434 1451
 Shell corrections according to Myers-Swiatecki                   7434 1451
