 *** ENDRESS - Merging source and resonance ENDF files            7434 1451
             Source ENDF W183_ib21g.t0                            7434 1451
          Resonance ENDF ..\resonance\w183jeff3.1mine_u.end       7434 1451
Added 1.8 b to capture and total background from 1.2 to 2.2 KeV   7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
RESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS (L. Leal, ORNL, Jan 2008)           7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
Resonance parameters from JENDL-3.3 were taken as a starter file. 7434 1451
Small adjustments to the parameters were made. The range was      7434 1451
extended to 2.2 keV.                                              7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
UNRESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS (ENDF/B-VII)                      7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
The average resonance parameters for the unresolved resonance     7434 1451
range were taken from ENDF/B-VII. They are used only for the      7434 1451
calculation of the self-shielding factors. The cross sections     7434 1451
are tabulated in File-3.                                          7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
RESONANCE COVARIANCE DATA (L. Leal, ORNL, Jan 2008)               7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
The procedure used to generate the resolved covariance data       7434 1451
with the SAMMY code is as follow:                                 7434 1451
 a) Retrieve best set of available resonance parameters.          7434 1451
 b) Convert the resonance parameters into the Reich-Moore form.   7434 1451
 c) Generate "experimental" cross sections for total, scattering, 7434 1451
    and capture cross sections with the NJOY code, for use as     7434 1451
    "experimental data" in SAMMY.                                 7434 1451
 d) Assign a global "experimental" uncertainty to the             7434 1451
    "experimental data." The uncertainties used were based on     7434 1451
    uncertainty in the thermal capture cross section and          7434 1451
    uncertainty in the capture resonance integrals.               7434 1451
 e) Run SAMMY code with the option to generate                    7434 1451
    resonance-covariances retroactively.                          7434 1451
 f) Convert the resonance-covariance results from SAMMY into      7434 1451
    the ENDF format for file 32 and MT=151.                       7434 1451
                                                                  7434 1451
The resulting resonance parameters and covariance were used in    7434 1451
the calculations of average cross sections and uncertainties.     7434 1451
The calculations were done with SAMMY, ERRORJ, and PUFF-IV codes. 7434 1451
The results of these three codes agreed very well.                7434 1451
